- **Boundary:** Driver command schema (escher-driver)
  - **What to validate:** A caller-built `Call` — a verb name and named argument values, each text, a whole number or a flag
  - **How (stack-specific):** `validate` checks a call against a closed `'static` table of twelve verbs in three levels — the seven asked of the held instance (`snapshot` — one optional `part`, its result `text` and, when the screen is read in parts, the counts `part` and `parts`; a screen over the snapshot budget read from part 1 with no `part`, a part past the last the empty text —, `click`, `type`, `press`, `advance`, `scroll`, `screenshot` — the sixth, taking one required `id`, joined at 2026-10-07-refusal-detection: a widening of this validated surface, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07; the seventh, taking one optional `id`, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, its result fields `width` and `height` (counts) and `png` (base64 text, `FieldKind::Png`, a tenth field kind) — the screen's pixels in band, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-12, «В самом ответе», relayed verbatim by the overseer), an eighth, `lint` (no argument, any argument refused `malformed` with `Fault::Unnamed`; one result field, `findings`, `FieldKind::Entries`, always present; refused `fonts-unavailable` before anything is read; running no step — a widening of this validated surface onto every ratified carrier, a ratified one) and, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, the three asked of the session itself (`start`, taking one required `app`, `status` and `stop` — a further widening of the surface, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option labels «Бинарник приложения, путь» · «Именованные флаги» · «Четыре класса»; the English wording is the overseer's), and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, the one asked of the tool itself, `help` (no argument; `Level::Tool`, its seven result fields fixed table text — a further widening of the surface, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-12, «help
 — десятый глагол», relayed verbatim by the overseer), which `validate` refuses as `unknown-verb` before their arguments are read and `validate_session` checks by the same rules, returning a typed `SessionCommand` (`Help` for `help`, any argument to it refused `malformed`, `Fault::Unnamed`); a session-level verb or `help` handed to `Session::run` is `unknown-verb`, its span recording the table's word — and seven argument kinds, each with its bound — `id` 1 to 1024 bytes of text, `text` 0 to 4096 bytes, `key` one name of a closed twelve-name list, `flag` true or false, `milliseconds` a whole number from 1 to 60000, the sixth, `name`, 1 to 32 bytes of `a-z`, `0-9` and `-`, and the seventh, `part`, a whole number from 1 to 1000 (`MAX_PART`) taken through `u32::try_from` (ten arguments across the table) — and returns a typed `Command` or a `Refusal`, one answer per call, the first failure in a fixed order: the verb by exact name (absent → `unknown-verb`), then the call's arguments in the order passed (a name the verb lacks, or a name passed twice → `malformed`), then the verb's arguments in the schema's order (required and absent, a value of another kind, a value outside its bound or a text that is no key name → `malformed`), each `malformed` naming the rule it broke; it has no `unwrap`, `expect`, `panic!`, `unreachable!` or index on anything a call supplies, reads no clock, and receives no `Session`, so a refused call changes nothing by construction; executed in process since 2026-10-07-act-by-id: `Session::run(&Call)` calls `validate` first and returns its refusal before anything else runs, and nothing public runs a `Command` that did not come from `validate`;
 an `id` — of `click`, `type`, `scroll` or, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `screenshot` — is then looked up on the screen as it reads now (the `id` row below), and one that names no element there is refused with nothing run, `stale` when the session's record of ids holds it and `not-found` when not; a `click` or a `type` on an element that cannot take it is refused with nothing run as well, with one answer, the first that holds in a fixed order — `disabled` (the snapshot reads the element not enabled), then `off-screen` (the centre of its bounds lies outside the viewport, or outside the visible part of a scrolling box that holds it), then `covered` (the hit at that point never reaches it) — and each refused call leaves the snapshot and both focus readings as they were, in both layout modes; `scroll` applies none of the three and says `in_view` in its result instead of refusing; `press` and `advance` are refused for no screen-level cause; all eight causes are returned by code, two by `validate` and six by the executor (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — `fonts-unavailable`, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, refusing a `screenshot` of an app with no font it can paint text with before anything is painted, and a `lint` of one before anything is read; a `screenshot` whose crop to the visible part of its element's bounds holds no pixel is refused `off-screen`, and every refused shot leaves the instance unchanged; `advance` is accepted on every session — inside one settled step it moves the session's clock, the harness's `VirtualClock` its documents read, by exactly the `ms` asked, then hands `ms` to the time step where the session's caller handed one, and the time it reports is exactly `ms` (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18); the executor has no `unwrap`, `expect`, `panic!` or `unreachable!` on anything a call supplies, reads no clock itself
 — its settled step's load wait, the session's, reads the wall clock (below) — and keeps no `NodeId` between calls — what the session does keep, since 2026-10-07-refusal-detection, is a record of id text (the `id` row below): at most 4096 ids, a count of ids and not the `text` bound of 4096 bytes above, fed from the session's own snapshots and never from a call's argument; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli external surfaces reach it, each through `validate` first — the session socket's `call` request, which a host decodes and runs through `Session::run` and nothing else, the `escher-session` command line, whose client checks a call before it sends it, so a call the schema refuses is answered there and reaches no session, and since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface an MCP `tools/call`, which the MCP server turns into a `Call` (a value of the wrong JSON kind refused `malformed` before anything runs) and runs through `Session::run` on the session it holds — with none held the call is validated first and answered `no-session` — answering `start`, `status`, `stop` and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, `help` itself after `validate_session` (packages/escher-driver/src/command.rs:32-60; packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:215-279): it is the check the three pass through, and an external-input surface from 2026-10-10-driver-cli on (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, with the crossing — «Бинарник приложения, путь» · «Именованные флаги» · «Четыре класса» — and its MCP carrier by his answer «Ратифицировать как есть», relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option labels; the English wording is the overseer's; until then no socket, CLI or MCP tool reached it);
 `Command`, `Call` and `ArgValue` derive `Debug`, which prints the id and the typed text they hold, and `Outcome` derives it too, printing the ids, accessible names and control values of its diff (a password's or a file input's value as the mask) and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, each diff node's three state readings (`selected` and `pressed`, each an optional boolean, and `invalid`, a boolean) and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, a changed node's `differs` (a `Vec<Reading>` of a closed eleven-variant enum) and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, a shot's PNG bytes (`Outcome::Shot`) and a lint's findings (`Outcome::Linted { findings }`, written by `to_json` alone as `{"findings":[…]}`, a finding `id` · `defect` · `bounds` then its reason's keys: stable ids, closed defect words and numbers only — no `NodeId`, page text, colour or control value) and a screen's part (`Outcome::Part { text, part, parts }`, its text the snapshot text's own lines, written by `to_json` alone as `{"text":…,"part":n,"parts":m}`), and the crate logs none of them and fields none — a state reading included: the command span keeps its eight fields at that chunk (`stand_act_spans`; `host_log` under both builds) — it writes an outcome in two places only, as a command's answer on the command line's stdout and, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, as an MCP tool result on the `mcp` role's stdout, by the ratified crossing: what it fields, since 2026-10-07-driver-command-spans, is one `tracing` span per call handed to `Session::run` — target `escher_driver`, name `command`, level INFO, built by hand with `tracing::info_span!` (no `#[instrument]`), entered before `validate` so a refusal is inside it
 — with eight fields, each unrecorded until it applies: `verb` (the verb table's own word, never the caller's verb text), `cause` (`Cause::name()` of a returned refusal), `settled`, `busy` (the schema's class word), `passes`, and `added` · `removed` · `changed` (the three list lengths of the returned diff) — fixed words, bools and counts only; never fielded: any `Command`, `Call`, `ArgValue`, `Outcome`, `Refusal` or `Fault`, any argument, the screen text or its length, a part's number or the part count, a shot's image, its size or its dimensions, a lint's findings or their count (a `screenshot`, a `lint` or a part read records `verb` and, refused, `cause`), the session's label, the record of ids, `in_view` or `advanced_ms`; the crate installs no subscriber and still reads no env var, and its executor, schema, validation and JSON writer and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, its `image` encoder read no clock, and none of them nor the session prints — the clocks are the host's, read on its accept loop for the idle expiry, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the MCP server's, read when a request arrives with a session held, and since 2026-10-20-load-wait the session's, read for the load wait alone (`Instant::now` and a sleep, bounded by `LOAD_WAIT`), and the writers its command line and the MCP server (the timings on a printed line are the sink's); since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the crate also fields a second span, `tool_call` under `escher_driver`, one per MCP `tools/call`, holding `tool` (the table's word) and `ending` (`accepted` · `refused` · `error`) only, the parent of `command` — answered by the founder, 2026-10-10, «Span с tool и ending», relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label, the English wording is the overseer's (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:118-121;
 packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:140-147), so with no subscriber the span is disabled and writes nothing, and under escher's sink it is one line per call at `info` or below and none at the default `warn` (§Logging & Monitoring) (packages/escher-driver/src/command.rs:248; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:96-111; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:113-298; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:302-341; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:408-498) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-command-and-refusal-schema/report.md, the executor at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/report.md, the detected causes, the session's record and the sixth verb at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md, the span and its fields at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md

- **Boundary:** Markup attributes
  - **What to validate:** `id` (stable element id)
  - **How (stack-specific):** Besides CSS matching and `getElementById`, a Dioxus document's `element_id` / `element_ids` read the HTML `id` as an element's author key only when it is non-empty, contains no `/` and is the first element in document pre-order to claim it; an empty, `/`-bearing or later-duplicate value gives no key and anchors nothing; an element with no key reads one of three `/`-bearing paths — an anchored path `{key}//{segment}` (then `/{segment}` per further DOM level) under the nearest element of its own component instance that reads an author key, else its component path, else its document path, a template root owned by another component instance restarting at that component's chain, so an anchor acts inside one component only; an author key holds no `/`, an anchored path is the only id holding `//`, and a component or document path has no empty segment, so no `id` can make two ids equal — a key spelled like a component name included (`Item//b:0` beside `Item/b:0`) — the anchored tier ratified by the founder (2026-10-06); a non-element, stale or detached node reads `None`, and no path panics; the id is computed on demand and escher's own code writes it to no log, DOM or vdom — an author-key id is the element's HTML `id`, though, which Stylo's own records carry (`style::*`, `selectors::matching`): those targets are outside the sink's allowlist, so since 2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist a host that installs escher's sink drops them whole and prints that value at no `RUST_LOG` level
 — the instrument's id needles found on stderr, before → after the drop: the `escher-session` binary on `crud` 15 of 15 → 0 at `debug` and at `trace`, the windowed `seven_guis_native` on Home 11 of 11 → 0 at `debug` and at `trace`, and 0 on both at the default level and at `info` before and after (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/evidence/by-level.md); under the `accessibility` feature `DioxusDocument::accessibility_tree` carries it as each element node's AccessKit `author_id` — never on a `TextRun`, the document root or the synthetic `Window` node, and never by indexing the slab with a tree id — so it leaves the process only through the platform accessibility adapter when an assistive technology is active, the crossing text runs and labels already take (ratified by the operator, 2026-10-06); since 2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff the adapter receives the tree on change as well as on its initial request — on a poll that reported work the windowed shell's `View::poll` takes the document's changed set (`BaseDocument::take_changed_nodes`) and, under `accessibility`, rebuilds the platform tree when the set it took was non-empty, where before that chunk the poll-time refresh did not run and the tree was built once — the same crossing and the same content classes (ids as `author_id`, accessible names), more often (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07; its windowed witness is still owed — no windowed run witnesses the refresh on the dev host); since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions the tree that crossing is handed is asserted headlessly on the stand in both layout modes
 — `Document::accessibility_tree` called through `&dyn blitz_dom::Document`, as `AccessibilityState::update_tree` calls it, equals the document's own `accessibility_tree()` node for node with the same focus and root, every `author_id` on it is its node's `DioxusDocument::element_id`, none empty, all digits or holding `0x`, and each lean task's tree carries at least its controls' ids — and the refresh's two halves are proven there too: after a drained changed set a Tab and an Enter each leave `has_changes()` true and that tree reads the new focus and the rewritten name (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:310-352; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:363-410 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions/report.md); what the platform adapter hands an assistive technology stays unread — the stand builds no adapter, kept so on the founder's F1 «Пока нет, перенести (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-14, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed by the overseer as his chosen option label, inputs#I2 of escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions), that witness owned by a `.andromeda/residuals.md` line (target: next); since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states the crossing carries a third content class, control states — `selected`, `toggled` and `invalid` on each element node whose markup states them, closed enums and booleans, never an attribute's value as typed (`toggled` from `aria-checked` on a checkable role and from `aria-pressed` on every other; the `aria-selected` · `aria-pressed` · `aria-checked` · `aria-invalid` row) — a widening ratified by the founder (2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Ратифицировать»;
 the English wording is the overseer's), its windowed witness owed like the refresh's: no check reads the three at the adapter on the dev host; since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync the names it carries include `aria-labelledby`'s computed text (the `aria-label` · `<label for>` row), and it carries a fourth content class, descriptions — `aria-description`'s own text and `aria-describedby`'s targets as `described_by` (the `aria-describedby` · `aria-description` row) — a widening by upstream merge ratified as upstream's behaviour by the founder (2026-10-17, «Утвердить оба (Рекомендую)», both sources confirmed by his «Подтвердить все 10 (Рекомендую)», 2026-10-18), its windowed witness owed like the states'; under the same feature `DioxusDocument::snapshot` is a second, in-process reader of that `author_id` — it takes no argument, copies the id verbatim into `SnapshotNode.id`, resolves each tree id through `BaseDocument::get_node` (never an index) and omits a node that does not resolve — and adds no crossing of its own: the snapshot has one text form, `Snapshot::to_text` (same feature; no JSON form, no `Display` impl, no parser of the text), which writes each node's id as a quoted `id=` field in `str`'s `Debug` form, so the field never holds a line break or a bare `"`; that text was returned to its caller only until 2026-10-10-driver-cli (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07) and no log or event carries the snapshot or its text — the one file that does is a kept check: since 2026-10-19-session-recording a recorded session's calls, the ids they named among them, and since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay each answer kept whole, a `snapshot`'s text and every diff included, a shot's pixels excepted, owner-only and never logged but for the two committed stand checks in git (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-19: F3 B, F1 A);
 since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the driver's `snapshot` command returns it through `Session::run` to the code that called `run` — `to_text`'s one caller outside the tests — and since 2026-10-10-driver-cli that caller can be a session host: a hosted `snapshot`'s answer carries the text, ids included, over the session socket (`ok v3 accepted <json>`) and onto the `escher-session` client's stdout as one line of JSON, the in-process text unchanged (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Сокет несёт команды», the English wording is the overseer's; the operator's 2026-10-07 answer that nothing of it goes on the socket is superseded) — so escher's own code now gives the id three exits — and, since 2026-10-19-session-recording, a fourth at rest, a kept check holding the ids a recorded session's calls named and, since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay, every id its kept answers read — owner-only, and in the two committed Counter checks under `tests/blitz-tests/checks/` in git (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-19) — the platform adapter, the driver's answers and, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, MCP tool results on the `escher-session mcp` role's stdout — an accepted `snapshot` the screen text itself — a paged one its JSON line `{"text","part","parts"}` holding the same text —, any other accepted call its JSON line (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, «Ратифицировать как есть», relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label; the English wording is the overseer's) — and an id a call names arrives also as an MCP tool's string `id` argument, bounded by `validate` inside `Session::run`; neither the id nor the snapshot carries a `NodeId`, `ElementId`, `ScopeId` or pointer; under the same feature `DioxusDocument::unkeyed_actionable` is a third in-process reader of the id
 — it takes no argument, takes ids from `element_ids()` and roles from `accessibility_tree`, resolves each node through `BaseDocument::get_node` and skips one that does not resolve, logs nothing and never panics, and returns an `UnkeyedActionable` (`node`, `id`, `tag`, `role`, `focusable`, `interactive_role`, `listener`) for each actionable element whose id holds a `/`; an entry holds the id, tag and role and never the element's text content, accessible name or an attribute value of that element, and its `node` field is a process-local `NodeId`, meaningful in process only; it adds no crossing of its own — no wire form, no log, event, socket or file, and no driver, CLI or MCP command yet (whether it becomes one is owned by a route entry) — the id's exits being the platform adapter, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli the driver's answers, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface MCP tool results and, since 2026-10-19-session-recording, a kept check's call targets and, since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay, its kept answers' ids; under the same feature `Snapshot::diff` is a fourth in-process reader of the id, through the snapshot model only — a pure function of two `Snapshot` values (no document access, no failure path, no log, no print) that copies ids into `DiffNode.id`, `DiffNode.parent` and `SnapshotDiff.removed`, holds no `NodeId`, `ElementId`, `ScopeId`, AccessKit id or pointer, and has no text form, `Display` impl, JSON form or parser of its own; since 2026-10-19-visual-lint escher-driver's `Session::lint` is a fifth reader of the id — it takes no argument, reads the snapshot and returns `Finding`s holding ids, closed defect words and numbers only (no `NodeId`, page text, colour or control value; a text control's value never measured), and crosses as the `lint` verb's answer (`Command::Lint` → `Outcome::Linted`, written `{"findings":[…]}`) on every ratified carrier
 — the socket's `call`, the command line, MCP and a kept check, kept whole — a ratified boundary widening, with no log site, print, span or field carrying a finding (its `command` span `verb` and, refused, `cause` only) and `VERBS` holding twelve; until 2026-10-10-driver-cli a diff was returned to its caller only (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07, with the snapshot text's answer), and since that chunk the driver's `Outcome::to_json` writes a returned diff as JSON — a node keyed by the schema's node fields in order — and an acting command's answer carries it over the session socket and onto the client's stdout (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Сокет несёт команды»; the English wording is the overseer's); no log or event carries a diff, and since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay a file only as a kept check's kept answer, owner-only and never logged, the two committed stand checks in git the one exception (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-19: F3 B, F1 A) — while, since 2026-10-07-driver-command-spans, the three list lengths of a diff the driver returns (`added` · `removed` · `changed`: counts only, no node, id, name or value) are recorded on the driver's command span, which escher's sink prints at `info` or below (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-09: the sentence stands, and it gains the clarification that a diff's content never reaches a log while its three sizes — the counts of added, removed and changed — may; the Driver command schema row; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md); since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the driver's five acting commands — `click`, `type`, `press`, `advance` and, since 2026-10-07-refusal-detection, `scroll` — return the diff of their one settled step through `Session::run` to the code that called `run` — `diff`'s one caller outside the tests
